 a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+36 & ={x}^{2}-(-36) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-(36{i}^{2}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-(6i)^{2} \\\\  & =(x+6i)(x-6i)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533865 true] [17592186262201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262202 13194139533865 true] [17592186262201 1000 #edb/ref 17592186262203 13194139533865 true] [17592186262201 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533865 true] [17592186262201 1041 "field-1" 13194139533865 true] [17592186262201 1104 #edb/ref 17592186262202 13194139533865 true] [17592186262201 1110 #uuid "dfc7747f-169a-5595-9235-eada96ab49f7" 13194139533865 true] [17592186262202 1034 "(x+6i)(x-6i)" 13194139533865 true] [17592186262202 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533865 true] [17592186262202 1111 #uuid "00c49189-8eb1-5585-975d-2410d1097426" 13194139533865 true] [17592186262203 1034 "(x+6)(x-6)" 13194139533865 true] [17592186262203 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533865 true] [17592186262203 1111 #uuid "1e2f06fd-8c5a-52a5-8f2d-6a112458cd7b" 13194139533865 true] [17592186262204 1017 #edb/ref 17592186262205 13194139533865 true] [17592186262204 1089 "q-319471" 13194139533865 true] [17592186262204 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533865 true] [17592186262204 1100 "Write ${x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}+25$ in factored form as $(a+bi)^{2}(a-bi)^{2}.$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n${x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}+25=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533865 true] [17592186262204 1113 #uuid "15785172-c630-5198-be0a-963b458e2faa" 13194139533865 true] [17592186262204 1145 "First, let's factor the expression as a perfect square trinomial in ${x}^{2}.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}+25 & ={({x}^{2})}^{2}+2\\cdot 5\\cdot ({x}^{2})+{5}^{2} \\\\  & ={({x}^{2}+5)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to factor the sum of squares in the parentheses. To do this, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we 